DESCRIPTION:Official TicketsResale Tickets \nThis post contains affiliate links. We may earn a commission at no extra cost to you. \nAbout Nate Bargatze\nNate Bargatze is one of the biggest names in stand-up comedy today. Known as “The Great American” of comedy\, the Nashville-born comedian has built a massive following through his clean\, relatable humor that appeals to audiences of all ages and backgrounds. \nBargatze has released multiple acclaimed Netflix specials including The Tennessee Kid\, The Greatest Average American\, and Hello World. His wholesome\, self-deprecating style and masterful storytelling have earned him comparisons to comedy legends like Brian Regan and Jim Gaffigan. \nThe Big Dumb Eyes World Tour is his biggest tour yet\, selling out arenas across the globe. Grand Rapids is getting two shows on August 1 — this is the 7:00 PM evening performance. \nEvent Details\nDate: Saturday\, August 1\, 2026 \nTime: 7:00 PM (Evening Show) \nVenue: Van Andel Arena\, 130 Fulton West\, Grand Rapids\, MI 49503 \nAge Restriction: All ages (family-friendly content) \nTicket Prices: Starting from $57 \nAbout Van Andel Arena\nVan Andel Arena is Grand Rapids’ largest and most iconic entertainment venue\, located at 130 Fulton West in the heart of downtown. With a capacity of approximately 12\,000\, it hosts the biggest concerts\, sporting events\, and comedy shows that come through West Michigan. \nThe arena features multiple seating levels including floor\, lower bowl\, and upper bowl sections\, multiple concession stands and bars\, and ample parking in nearby downtown structures. The venue is easily accessible from US-131 and I-196\, and is surrounded by downtown Grand Rapids’ vibrant restaurant and bar scene. \nAn evening comedy show at Van Andel Arena is the perfect Saturday night out for the whole family or a group of friends. \nWhat to Expect\nThis is a solo headline stand-up show featuring Nate Bargatze performing his full set. Expect approximately 75–90 minutes of clean\, hilarious comedy that the whole family can enjoy. Bargatze’s storytelling style draws you in from the first minute and keeps you laughing until the very end. \nThis is the evening show at 7:00 PM. A matinee show at 3:00 PM is also available on the same day. Arrive early to find your seats and enjoy the arena atmosphere before the show begins. \nTicket Information\nPrice Range: Starting from $57 (fees may apply) \nSecure your seats through the official Ticketmaster link or find resale tickets through VividSeats for flexible options. \nOfficial TicketsResale Tickets
